[COMMAND]:      image.update.production
[PACKAGE]:      IMAGE
[USE]:          dock -image update.production

[OUT]:          Stops the container service in the current directory (production containers only), 
                disables the service, deletes the container's parent image, starts the container 
                again forcing a new parent image to be downloaded, enables the service again, 
                starts it, and returns the state of it.

[ACTIONS]:      dock -service stop
                dock -service disable
                dock -stop -del
                docker image rm $IMAGE_FULL_NAME
                dock -start
                dock -service enable
                dock -service start
                dock -service status

[NOTES]:        More information available in the image.sh script.
